# kickoff-club — agent rules

Read `docs/architecture/README.md` and linked docs before feature work.

## Layers (strict)

`ui` (React, `src/app/`) → `api` (`src/app/api/v1/`) → `domain` (`src/modules/*/domain/`) → `infra` (db, mail).

**Domain MUST NOT import `react`, `next/*`, or route handler types.**

## Folders

- Modules: `src/modules/{auth,groups,matches,rsvps,notifications}/`
- Shared: `src/lib/` (config Zod boot, errors, logging)
- Persistence: Drizzle schema in `src/lib/db/`; forward-only SQL in `drizzle/` (`YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_description.sql`)

## Process gates

- Non-trivial features require an approved OpenSpec change under `openspec/changes/`.
- REST JSON at `/api/v1`; conventional commits; no secrets in git.
- Package manager: **pnpm** + committed lockfile.

## Conventions (mandatory topics)

Error handling, transactionality, domain modeling, logging/redaction, design patterns, testing (unit/integration/e2e + CI), external integrations (SMTP retries/timeouts), frontend a11y/states — all defined under `docs/architecture/`. Follow them.

## Current pin (v0.1.0)

Must-scope shipped: auth sessions, groups/invites/last-organizer RBAC, one-off and weekly series matches, RSVP capacity + waitlist promotion, notifications/no-shows, Playwright e2e, README + demo seed.

Do **not** implement Should-scope items (password reset, match list pagination, this-and-future series cancel, notification preferences, unmark no-show) unless a new OpenSpec change proposes them. See `openspec/backlog/should-scope.md`.
